     3| *
     4| * Sends a single SMS via the AWS SNS `Publish` API (短信) using a SigV4-signed
     5| * HTTPS request — no new dependencies, same signing pattern as the SES module.
     6| *
     7| * AWS SNS gives new accounts a small monthly free tier of outbound SMS (~200
     8| * messages in the US on the SMS sandbox tier before spending past the free
     9| * grant), which is more than enough for the owner-only recovery flow.
    10| *
    11| * Credentials come from the existing AWS env (AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID /
    12| * AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY / AWS_REGION / AWS_SESSION_TOKEN). The destination
    13| * phone is resolved in this order: explicit caller override →
    14| * IVX_OWNER_RECOVERY_PHONE env var. The sender ID is IVXOwner.
    15| *
    16| * SAFETY: callers must enforce owner approval / allowlist before invoking this.
    17| * This module only performs the transport — it never decides whether a message
    18| * may be sent. Owner recovery codes are short-lived (5 min) and rate-limited.
    19| */
