     1|/**
     2| * IVX Owner Login Recovery via SMS — secondary owner access path.
     3| *
     4| * Provides a redundant, AWS-SNS-backed SMS recovery link so the owner can
     5| * always get back into the app even when the primary email/password Supabase
     6| * login path is broken. The flow is:
     7| *
     8| *   1. Owner (or operator) calls POST /api/ivx/owner-recovery/request
     9| *      with the owner email. The backend resolves the registered owner phone
    10| *      (from the auth user or IVX_OWNER_RECOVERY_PHONE env), generates a
    11| *      6-digit code, persists it with a 5-minute TTL, and texts it via SNS.
    12| *   2. Owner receives the SMS, enters the code on the phone, which calls
    13| *      POST /api/ivx/owner-recovery/verify with email + code. On success the
    14| *      backend returns a short-lived recovery token and (optionally) repairs
    15| *      the owner password to the value submitted so the owner can sign in
    16| *      immediately.
    17| *   3. GET /api/ivx/owner-recovery/status exposes SNS readiness (no secrets).
    18| *
    19| * Security:
    20| *   - Codes are 6 digits, single-use, expire after 5 minutes.
    21| *   - Max 3 attempts per code, max 5 requests per phone per 15 minutes.
    22| *   - Owner email must match the allowlist (same gate as owner registration).
    23| *   - Recovery token is a random 256-bit secret, single-use, 10-minute TTL.
    24| *
    25| * Twilio integration remains pending; AWS SNS is the active transport.
    26| */
